@nsobid-FF773E90972D544EB79406EAA65396D53C43EFB9

# Super Mario Bros. Wonder 1.2.1 - 4096x4096 depth shadow map

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces the sun cascade shadow map to 4096x4096 so shadow edges stop
// being blocky.
//
// The size is not a constant: gsys::ModelSceneConfig exposes it as the
// env parameters depth_shadow_tex_width / _height, and the in-code
// defaults are placeholders (1024 and the sentinel -1), so each stage's
// env archive supplies the real values. The per-frame shadow draw then
// scales the configured size by the viewport ratio and takes a minimum,
// which only ever shrinks it, so raising the render resolution alone
// changes nothing.
//
// Overwriting the two config reads with immediates sidesteps both: the
// minimum keeps the immediate exactly for any viewport at or above the
// reference size, and the result is the same in every stage.
//
// The shadow map is a cascade texture array allocated per frame from the
// agl::utl::DynamicTextureAllocator pool, and cost scales with the square
// of the size, so 4096 is 16x the memory of the 1024 default. The
// stock 96 MB pool can run out on its own; install one of the resolution
// mods alongside this, which raise that pool. Do not duplicate the pool
// offset here.

@enabled
// gsys::ModelSceneConfig::depth_shadow_tex_width / _height reads in the
// per-frame depth shadow draw.
0011694C 0C008252   // MOVZ W12,#4096 (was LDR W12,[X8,#0x16A8])
00116970 08008252   // MOVZ W8,#4096  (was LDR W8,[X8,#0x16C8])
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Super Mario Bros. Wonder 1.2.1
// (sead + agl/gsys, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped, so both
// sites were located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
